    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Proclaimed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> on 1 October 1949 after the Communist victory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war">Chinese Civil War</a>.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-leap-forward">Great Leap Forward</a> famine and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultural-revolution">Cultural Revolution</a> were among the greatest human catastrophes of the century.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deng-xiaoping">Deng Xiaoping</a>’s reforms from 1978 combined market economics with one-party rule and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> a global economic power.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanyu-pinyin">Hanyu Pinyin</a>, the romanisation now used worldwide to spell Chinese names, was adopted by the People’s Republic in 1958.</p></aside>
